n arithmetic (MBB alphalens -2.9245% -> -2.9%; alphalens portfolio +0.8985% / alpha +4.4915pp -> +0.90% / +4.49pp; converge portfolio -1.2450% / alpha +2.9608pp -> -1.24% / +2.96pp) and generated the live report sections, whose printed numbers matched all six including the +0.81pp vs-production figure. Reproduced all 6 B1 counts and all 8 B2 counts from my own BigQuery queries — exact. Rebuilt the reverse-proof independently (6 fails / 4 positions, 9/9 untouched) — exact. Verified EXPLAIN_TOL plateau [1e-4, 0.08] by sweep.", "killer_objection": "C3's gate is unreachable in production, so it protects nothing today. paper_entry_gate() runs only via run_gate(report_path), whose sole production caller is send_report_email.py — but the report carrying the paper sections, [REDACTED]eport.py (crontab '0 23 * * 0-4' = 06:00 ICT Mon-Fri), posts directly to Discord via notify_thread.sh:123 and never writes a .md file. No .md anywhere in the repo contains PAPER_MARKERS, and send_plan_report.sh / eod_trading_report.sh reference neither report module. Worse, the payload's stated rationale ('[REDACTED] carries the paper section but no account label IN THE FILENAME, so the old early-exit skipped it entirely') presupposes it is a file traversing the gate — a false premise about the production path. The mechanism is correct and demonstrably blocks in both directions; it simply never runs on the channel where these numbers reach the user. Anyone reading this finding would believe the paper numbers are now gated. They are not.", "recommended_reruns": ["Wire the gate into the channel that actually carries the numbers: have [REDACTED]eport.py either call report_return_gate.paper_entry_gate() on its assembled message before notify_thread.sh (fail-closed, do not post on CHAN), or write a dated .md and route it through send_report_email.py. Until then state plainly in the report that the paper leg is NOT active in production.", "Apply B4's own fix to report_return_gate.py: make its selfcheck print a machine-counted total (len(ran)) like the other two files, then correct '+12 ca' to the true +11 in the report and in the af1e201b commit-message narrative.", "Add an ABSOLUTE cache-freshness floor alongside the relative stale_years(): a wholly frozen bq_cache flags nothing today, and the only thing that catches it (T1) lives behind the gate that does not run.", "Before wiring oshares_live.py: broaden the anchor cross-check well beyond HAH/FPT/NAF/DHG (the 145/75 hard-look-ahead population is the natural sampling frame) and re-check MAX(ingested_at) on corporate_action on [REDACTED] as the report already schedules.", "When quoting the paper alphas anywhere downstream, carry the n and the panel-curation caveat; +4.49pp / +2.96pp / +0.81pp over ~6 weeks on 4 and 9 hand-picked names is not evidence of edge.", "Optional but worth a line in the docstring: accrue-only assumes the right LAPSES, yet quyen mua is frequently transferable on HOSE and selling it needs no cash account — so accrue-only is the conservative floor, not the only defensible convention. Both numbers are already printed side by side, which is what makes this acceptable."], "summary": "Every measurable claim in this finding reproduced in my own environment, and several reproduced more strongly than claimed — the TERP inversion matches to float equality (404/485), not merely six decimals, and I re-derived the accrue-only factor 0.835955 from first principles rather than accepting it. All 6 B1 look-ahead counts and all 8 B2 fail-closed counts came out exact from my own BigQuery queries; the three headline returns, the reverse-proof (6 fails / 4 positions, 9/9 untouched), the crosscheck (T1 13/13, T2 4/4) and all three selfchecks reproduced exactly. EXPLAIN_TOL=0.001 is a real plateau spanning [1e-4, 0.08], not a tuned point. The arithmetic and the fail-closed behaviours are sound, and the patches do what they say. Two defects: the claimed '+12 new cases' is +11 by machine count — the very hand-typed-count error B4 declares closed, because that fix was never applied to report_return_gate.py; and, materially, the C3 gate cannot fire in production, since the only report carrying the paper sections posts straight to Discord from [REDACTED]eport.py and never becomes a file for run_gate() to read. The finding's rationale for C3 rests on a false premise about that data path, and readers would wrongly conclude the paper numbers are now protected. I confirm rather than refute because the finding explicitly declines to claim closure and lists its open items, oshares_live is genuinely unwired, and nothing here sits on the live money path — but confidence is medium, not high, until C3's gate is connected to the channel it was built to guard."}
